::STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q01::
Question ID: STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.BVM.3
Question:
Actual value is 90 and predicted value is 84. What is the residual?
{
=A. 6#Residual = actual - predicted = 90 - 84 = 6.
~B. -6#This reverses the subtraction. Use actual - predicted.
~C. 174#This adds the values instead of subtracting.
~D. 84#This is the predicted value, not the residual.
}

::STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q02::
Question ID: STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.BVM.3
Question:
Actual value is 52 and predicted value is 60. How should the residual be interpreted?
{
~A. The model underpredicted by 8#The residual is negative, so the model predicted too high.
=B. The model overpredicted by 8#Residual = 52 - 60 = -8, so the actual value was 8 below the prediction.
~C. The model predicted exactly#An exact prediction would have residual 0.
~D. The residual is 112#This adds actual and predicted instead of subtracting.
}

::STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q03::
Question ID: STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.BVM.3
Question:
What does a residual of 0 mean?
{
=A. The actual value equals the predicted value#Residual 0 means actual - predicted = 0.
~B. The model is always perfect#One residual of 0 does not prove the whole model is perfect.
~C. The actual value is below the prediction#A negative residual would mean actual is below predicted.
~D. The predicted value is missing#A residual cannot be calculated without a predicted value.
}

::STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q04::
Question ID: STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.BVM.3
Question:
What residual pattern supports using a linear model?
{
~A. A clear curved pattern#A curve suggests a line may not fit well.
~B. All residuals getting larger in one direction#That pattern suggests the line is missing structure.
~C. All residuals are positive#All positive residuals mean the model is consistently underpredicting.
=D. Random scatter around 0#Random scatter around 0 supports a linear fit.
}

::STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q05::
Question ID: STAT_U03_L03_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.BVM.3
Question:
What residual pattern suggests a line may not fit well?
{
~A. Residuals both above and below 0 with no pattern#That supports a linear model.
~B. Several residuals close to 0#Small residuals suggest close predictions.
=C. A curved pattern in the residuals#A curve means the relationship may not be linear.
~D. One residual equal to 0#One exact prediction does not show poor fit.
}
